WEBVTT

00:29.017 --> 00:32.353
- What's that?
- Cheat sheet Faraday drew for me.

00:32.395 --> 00:35.231
You don't know where your boat is?

00:35.273 --> 00:36.774
I know where it is.

00:49.537 --> 00:52.457
Why are you flying directly
into the thunderhead?

00:52.499 --> 00:55.376
Why don't you just sit back
and let me do my job?

01:03.760 --> 01:04.844
Is that Penelope?

01:06.930 --> 01:10.350
She told Charlie she didn't know
about this boat, correct?

01:10.391 --> 01:11.476
Aye.

01:11.518 --> 01:13.926
What do you expect to find
when you get there?

01:14.020 --> 01:15.219
Answers.

01:32.247 --> 01:33.331
Damn it!

01:41.506 --> 01:42.924
Hold on!

01:46.052 --> 01:48.544
On your sodding feet!

01:48.596 --> 01:50.598
Move, move, move!

01:52.767 --> 01:55.228
What are you waiting for, Hume?

02:00.692 --> 02:02.569
What's the matter, Hume?

02:02.610 --> 02:04.936
Did you not hear me?

02:04.988 --> 02:07.949
I'm sorry, sir.
I was having a dream, sir.

02:07.991 --> 02:09.909
You were having a dream, were you?

02:09.951 --> 02:13.486
What were you dreaming about?
That it took you so sodding long

02:13.538 --> 02:15.540
to get to your mark?!

02:18.376 --> 02:19.878
I was in a helicopter, sir.

02:20.920 --> 02:23.381
And there was a storm, sir, and...

02:23.465 --> 02:27.510
And... I don't remember the rest, sir.

02:28.595 --> 02:31.931
Well, at least it was
a bloody military dream.

02:33.892 --> 02:36.561
Right! All of you!

02:36.603 --> 02:39.355
In the yard, four minutes!

02:39.397 --> 02:43.776
And you can thank Private Hume
for having to do it in double time.

02:43.818 --> 02:45.695
Move!

02:45.737 --> 02:47.071
- One, two...
- Three!

02:47.155 --> 02:48.823
- One, two, three...
- Four!

02:48.865 --> 02:50.909
- One, two, three...
- Five!

02:50.950 --> 02:53.192
One hundred crunches.

02:53.244 --> 02:55.121
Go, go, go, go, go!

02:55.955 --> 02:58.082
One, two, three...

02:58.124 --> 03:00.449
I hope your dream
was worth this, mate.

03:00.502 --> 03:02.827
Sorry, pal. Just...

03:02.879 --> 03:06.664
I've never had a dream so vivid.
It was like I was actually there.

03:06.716 --> 03:09.125
You got something to say, Hume?

03:09.177 --> 03:10.595
I asked you a question!

03:15.266 --> 03:16.768
We're almost through it.

03:16.810 --> 03:18.436
I see daylight.

03:23.858 --> 03:26.183
What do you think you're doing?
Desmond.

03:26.236 --> 03:27.695
Hey, you all right?

03:28.822 --> 03:29.906
Who are you?

03:31.491 --> 03:33.576
How do you know my name?

03:54.139 --> 03:55.421
Here you go.

04:01.312 --> 04:03.857
All right, they took off a day ago.

04:03.898 --> 04:07.235
- Why haven't we heard from them?
- I'm gonna tell you again,

04:07.277 --> 04:09.435
as I've been telling you, I don't know!

04:09.487 --> 04:12.615
You heard the same thing as I did
when we called the boat.

04:12.657 --> 04:16.494
- What makes you think I know anything?
- Because you're not worried.

04:16.536 --> 04:19.247
- Excuse me?
- Your boat's 40 miles off the coast.

04:19.372 --> 04:22.292
Should've taken them, what,
20 minutes to get there?

04:22.333 --> 04:23.710
Why aren't you worried?

04:23.751 --> 04:26.327
Should I wring my hands together

04:26.379 --> 04:29.997
- and whisper a prayer on their behalf?
- Hey, hey, hey. Come on.

04:30.049 --> 04:32.510
Maybe we should just tell them.

04:34.471 --> 04:35.847
Tell us what?

04:35.889 --> 04:39.809
Dan, let's not confuse anyone.

04:39.851 --> 04:44.022
Well, Daniel,
maybe if you talk real slow,

04:44.063 --> 04:45.773
we'll be able to follow.

04:49.527 --> 04:53.198
Your perception of how long
your friends have been gone...

04:54.240 --> 04:58.536
...it's not necessarily how long
they've actually been gone.

05:00.455 --> 05:02.916
- What does that mean?
- This is a mistake.

05:04.042 --> 05:06.044
It'll be fine, it'll be fine.

05:06.085 --> 05:08.838
As long as Frank flew
on the bearings I gave him.

05:08.880 --> 05:11.633
If he stayed on it, it'll be fine.

05:11.716 --> 05:13.426
And what if he didn't?

05:14.677 --> 05:17.430
Then there might be side effects.

05:20.767 --> 05:22.018
We're at 2,000 feet. Sit!

05:22.060 --> 05:23.937
- What am I doing here?
- What's going on?

05:23.978 --> 05:26.815
- Something's wrong with Desmond.
- Hold him in his seat!

05:26.856 --> 05:28.775
- I'm trying!
- Let go of me!

05:28.817 --> 05:31.694
Keep him away from the stick!
We'll be there in two minutes!

06:22.078 --> 06:23.997
What are you doing back?
Who are they?

06:24.038 --> 06:25.582
Survivors of 815.

06:26.958 --> 06:30.128
You dropped them here.
What the hell were you thinking?

06:30.920 --> 06:32.714
- Where am I?
- Just take it easy.

06:32.797 --> 06:35.008
Who are you people?
What am I doing here?

06:35.049 --> 06:36.843
- Who are you?
- My friend has...

06:36.885 --> 06:39.012
I'm not your friend! I don't know you!

06:39.053 --> 06:41.264
I don't know you!

06:42.474 --> 06:45.602
- When did he start doing this?
- He was fine when we took off.

06:45.643 --> 06:49.345
We hit some weather... Faraday said
as long as I stayed on the vector...

06:49.439 --> 06:50.523
OK. Go.

06:51.566 --> 06:54.652
Wait, wait, wait.
What's your name, my friend?

06:56.112 --> 06:58.114
- Sayid.
- OK, Sayid.

06:58.156 --> 07:00.825
We're gonna take your buddy
down to the sick bay.

07:00.867 --> 07:03.620
- I'm going with him.
- Let a doctor look at him first

07:03.703 --> 07:05.413
then you can come down.

07:05.455 --> 07:07.123
You got my word on that, OK?

07:15.173 --> 07:17.217
- All right.
- Listen to me.

07:17.258 --> 07:20.553
This is a mistake, right?
I don't know these people.

07:20.595 --> 07:23.139
- I understand.
- No, this is wrong!

07:23.181 --> 07:26.226
I'm not supposed to be here!

07:26.267 --> 07:28.978
Twenty, 21, 22...

07:29.020 --> 07:31.564
"Here"? Here what?

07:31.606 --> 07:34.317
What the hell are you doing
on your feet?

07:34.359 --> 07:36.934
Are you finished with your crunches

07:36.986 --> 07:38.488
because you want to run?!

07:38.530 --> 07:42.450
Right! Squad, on your feet!

07:44.536 --> 07:46.204
Right face!

07:46.246 --> 07:49.749
Ten kilometres! Go, go, go, go, go!

07:49.791 --> 07:52.877
Get moving, or so help me
I'll kill you myself!

07:59.717 --> 08:02.126
What the hell's the matter
with you, Des?

08:02.178 --> 08:04.264
If I told you, you'd think I was crazy.

08:04.305 --> 08:06.766
I already know you're crazy.

08:07.934 --> 08:12.105
This morning, when I was
in the yard doing crunches...

08:14.732 --> 08:16.276
...I left.

08:16.317 --> 08:18.153
What do you mean you "left"?

08:20.029 --> 08:22.907
I was on a boat.

08:22.949 --> 08:26.244
And then I was back here,
right where I started.

08:26.286 --> 08:28.496
Des, if you're trying to get tossed...

08:28.538 --> 08:30.999
Billy, I'm telling you the truth, man.

08:33.001 --> 08:36.004
Who else was on this... boat?

08:36.045 --> 08:38.006
Anyone you recognise?

08:40.091 --> 08:41.374
Penny.

08:44.762 --> 08:47.255
There was a photo.
Penny was in the photo.

08:48.349 --> 08:51.102
Oi, Des! Where are you going?

09:00.778 --> 09:02.572
Thanks for this morning, Hume.

09:09.871 --> 09:11.206
Watch your step.

09:12.081 --> 09:14.657
Watch it. Watch your step. Take it easy.

09:16.294 --> 09:17.378
I'm not here.

09:17.420 --> 09:19.964
This... This isn't happening.

09:20.006 --> 09:23.843
You are here, and this is happening.

09:23.927 --> 09:27.712
- Look, we're gonna take care of you.
- What am I doing here?

09:27.764 --> 09:31.017
- It's all right. You're gonna be OK.
- Who are you people?

09:31.059 --> 09:34.760
Well, my name is Keamy,
and this is Omar.

09:34.813 --> 09:38.316
I'm from Vegas, he's from Florida.
But as for where we are...

09:38.358 --> 09:40.193
We last ported in Fiji.

09:41.361 --> 09:44.113
So at least we know
we're still in the Pacific.

09:49.869 --> 09:53.373
All right, my friend.
You just relax, OK?

09:53.414 --> 09:54.874
We're gonna go get the doc,

09:54.916 --> 09:57.544
and he's gonna want to ask you
some questions

09:57.585 --> 10:00.505
- to help us sort all this out.
- What do you mean, sort out?

10:00.547 --> 10:02.841
What do you mean?
I'm not supposed to be here!

10:02.882 --> 10:05.885
I'm not supposed to be here!
Open this door!

10:05.927 --> 10:08.502
- Open this door!
- Hey!

10:11.349 --> 10:13.393
Hey, hey.

10:17.605 --> 10:21.693
It's happening to you too, isn't it?

10:57.061 --> 11:00.596
What's happening to Desmond?
Your friends know what's wrong.

11:00.648 --> 11:04.350
- If they do, they're not sharing.
- We'll share we took off at dusk

11:04.402 --> 11:06.696
and landed in the middle of the day.

11:09.282 --> 11:12.869
Listen, I don't know
what's happening to your buddy.

11:12.911 --> 11:15.455
But you gotta trust me
when I tell you this:

11:15.497 --> 11:17.738
I am trying to help you.

11:17.832 --> 11:21.085
You want to help me?
Give me your phone.

11:21.127 --> 11:23.369
Let me call my people.

11:23.505 --> 11:26.466
You give me that weapon,
and I'll give you this phone.

11:34.390 --> 11:37.727
Be quick.
Don't go trying to call Baghdad.

11:37.769 --> 11:39.927
Those phones only call each other.

11:47.987 --> 11:50.824
- Hello?
- <i>Jack</i>, <i>it's Sayid.</i>

11:50.865 --> 11:52.700
<i>I'm on the freighter.</i>

11:52.742 --> 11:54.744
Are you OK? Where have you been?

11:54.786 --> 11:57.278
Something happened during the flight...

11:57.330 --> 11:59.655
...and now Desmond's in their sick bay.

11:59.707 --> 12:02.335
Hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on.

12:02.377 --> 12:04.170
All right, you're on speaker.

12:04.212 --> 12:07.132
<i>On the helicopter</i>,
<i>something happened to Desmond.</i>

12:07.173 --> 12:10.135
He doesn't appear to recognise me
or know where he is.

12:12.011 --> 12:13.294
Side effects?

12:15.682 --> 12:17.517
Wait, your friend Desmond,

12:17.559 --> 12:21.855
has he recently been exposed
to high levels of radiation

12:21.896 --> 12:23.940
or electromagnetism?

12:27.026 --> 12:28.862
OK, look, we don't know why,

12:28.903 --> 12:31.030
but going to and coming from the island

12:31.114 --> 12:34.815
some people can get a little confused.

12:34.868 --> 12:38.163
So, what, is this amnesia?

12:41.791 --> 12:43.710
No. This is not amnesia.

12:45.920 --> 12:48.162
Hey. Hey.

12:48.256 --> 12:50.884
Hey! Can you hear me?

12:52.051 --> 12:53.303
Are you all right?

12:53.344 --> 12:55.096
Hello?

12:58.766 --> 13:01.175
I was just on a Ferris wheel.

13:05.273 --> 13:10.570
See, Ray? I'm not crazy.
It's happening to him too, Ray.

13:11.654 --> 13:13.239
It's gonna happen to you.

13:13.281 --> 13:15.241
It's gonna happen to all of us.

13:15.283 --> 13:18.369
Everyone. Once we start heading
to that island again.

13:18.411 --> 13:20.497
Would you please step aside?

13:21.080 --> 13:23.625
No, no... Ray, no.

13:23.666 --> 13:25.627
I need you to relax for a minute.

13:25.668 --> 13:29.120
No! No, it's not gonna stop it, Ray.
Nothing can stop it, Ray!

13:29.172 --> 13:31.132
Nothing can stop this...!

13:36.221 --> 13:39.557
- And how are you feeling?
- What the bloody hell is going on?!

13:39.599 --> 13:43.353
- I understand you're disoriented...
- You won't stick me with that!

13:43.394 --> 13:45.605
I don't want to stick you with anything.

13:45.647 --> 13:48.222
If it's OK, I just want
to check your eyes.

13:50.485 --> 13:53.738
- Why?
- So I can help you.

14:04.332 --> 14:05.708
What's your name?

14:08.378 --> 14:09.796
Desmond.

14:11.840 --> 14:13.039
Desmond.

14:15.718 --> 14:17.877
Why don't you tell me
the last thing you remember?

14:51.004 --> 14:52.505
<i>Hello?</i>

14:54.340 --> 14:55.925
Penny?

14:58.219 --> 14:59.888
<i>What do you want</i>, <i>Desmond?</i>

15:01.222 --> 15:02.849
Penny, listen, I'm...

15:03.600 --> 15:05.351
I'm in trouble.

15:06.561 --> 15:08.719
I think something's happened to me.

15:09.522 --> 15:13.359
I'm confused and...
I need to see you.

15:15.695 --> 15:18.531
<i>You broke off with me</i>
<i>and then you joined the army</i>,

15:18.573 --> 15:22.786
<i>and now you call with some expectation</i>
<i>I still care about you?</i>

15:22.827 --> 15:25.403
<i>Yeah</i>, <i>I'd say you are confused</i>,
<i>Desmond.</i>

15:25.455 --> 15:27.665
No, I'm not. It's...

15:27.707 --> 15:30.710
Look, I've got two days leave
starting tonight.

15:31.878 --> 15:34.287
- Can I... can I come and see you?
- <i>No.</i>

15:34.339 --> 15:37.842
<i>No. And don't bother showing up</i>
<i>at the flat either. I've moved.</i>

15:37.884 --> 15:39.260
Moved? Where?

15:39.302 --> 15:41.221
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

15:41.262 --> 15:44.682
<i>Look</i>, <i>Desmond</i>, <i>I'm going to go.</i>

15:44.724 --> 15:47.727
- <i>Please don't call me again.</i>
- No, listen, Penny, I...

15:47.769 --> 15:48.853
...need you.

15:53.107 --> 15:56.069
Did you just experience something,
Desmond?

15:58.947 --> 16:02.398
Frank, you're not supposed
to be here, definitely not with him.

16:02.450 --> 16:05.902
Sorry, but I got Faraday calling.
He needs to talk to this guy...

16:05.954 --> 16:10.125
- Faraday's not talking to my patient.
- He's not your patient!

16:10.166 --> 16:11.876
Give Desmond the phone.

16:12.961 --> 16:14.712
Give him the phone now!

16:19.717 --> 16:21.678
- Hello?
- Desmond.

16:21.719 --> 16:25.932
Desmond, my name is Daniel Faraday.
We met yesterday before you took off,

16:25.974 --> 16:28.299
but I'm guessing
you don't remember that.

16:28.351 --> 16:30.843
- Took off... What?
- <i>We don't have long to talk</i>,

16:30.895 --> 16:34.347
so I need you to tell me
what year you think it is.

16:34.399 --> 16:37.402
What do you mean what year
do I think...? It's 1996.

16:41.948 --> 16:46.244
All right. Desmond, look,
you gotta tell me, where are you?

16:46.286 --> 16:49.289
I'm... I'm in some kind of sick bay.

16:49.330 --> 16:52.459
No, not right now, Desmond.
Where are you supposed to be?

16:52.500 --> 16:54.586
Where are you in 1996?

16:54.627 --> 16:57.714
I'm at Camp Millar.
It's a Royal Scots regiment.

16:57.755 --> 16:59.591
<i>It's just north of Glasgow.</i>

16:59.632 --> 17:02.844
- Dan, you might...
- No, no, I'm thinking, I'm thinking.

17:04.012 --> 17:07.015
Desmond, listen,
when it happens again,

17:07.098 --> 17:08.766
I need you to get on a train.

17:09.434 --> 17:11.144
<i>Get on a train and go to Oxford</i>,

17:11.186 --> 17:14.939
Oxford University, Queen's College
Physics Department.

17:14.981 --> 17:16.983
What? Why?

17:18.276 --> 17:21.613
Because I need you to find me.

17:28.161 --> 17:30.246
- Where is it? Where is it?
- What?

17:30.288 --> 17:31.831
My journal, my journal.

17:31.873 --> 17:34.115
I need my journal,
or I won't believe him.

17:34.167 --> 17:37.462
- Why does he think he's in 1996?
- I don't know.

17:37.504 --> 17:39.745
It's unpredictable.
It's a random effect.

17:39.798 --> 17:42.675
Sometimes the displacement's
a couple hours, sometimes years.

17:42.717 --> 17:44.844
Wait, this has happened before?

17:44.886 --> 17:47.764
The phone, now, please. Thank you.

17:47.806 --> 17:50.517
- Desmond, are you still there?
- Hey, doc!

17:50.558 --> 17:52.769
Talk to him! I can't hold them for long.

17:52.811 --> 17:55.104
Yes! Yes, I'm here.

17:55.146 --> 17:57.982
OK, listen, when you find me
at Queen's College,

17:58.024 --> 18:02.028
I need you to tell me
to set the device to 2.342.

18:02.070 --> 18:04.948
- What?
- <i>You got it? 2.342.</i>

18:04.989 --> 18:07.481
It must be oscillating at 11 hertz.

18:07.534 --> 18:12.831
- <i>You got it</i>, <i>Desmond?</i>
- 2.342. Oscillate...

18:12.872 --> 18:16.574
<i>Just remember that.</i>
<i>2.342 at 11 hertz</i>, <i>all right?</i>

18:16.626 --> 18:20.578
One more thing, Desmond.
If the numbers don't convince me

18:20.630 --> 18:24.582
I need you to tell me
that you know about Eloise.

18:28.012 --> 18:29.639
Easy, easy!

18:29.681 --> 18:32.350
<i>Desmond? Tell me that you know</i>
<i>about Eloise...</i>

19:03.339 --> 19:07.469
Original, the opposite of derivative.

19:07.510 --> 19:10.680
I am the one for you to impress,
Mr Hollister.

19:10.763 --> 19:14.350
I'm not impressed.
So go, go try again.

19:16.686 --> 19:19.230
Sorry. Are you Daniel Faraday?

19:20.607 --> 19:24.475
- You are?
- Sorry. I'm Desmond Hume,

19:24.569 --> 19:27.030
and I was told I could find you here.

19:27.781 --> 19:31.618
I think I've... just been to the future.

19:34.913 --> 19:36.195
- The future?
- Yes.

19:36.247 --> 19:41.586
I spoke to you there. You told me
to come here to Oxford to find you.

19:42.504 --> 19:44.214
You said you'd help me.

19:44.297 --> 19:47.300
Why didn't I just help you there,
in the future?

19:47.342 --> 19:48.802
Sorry?

19:48.843 --> 19:52.138
Why would I put you through
the headache of time travel.

19:52.180 --> 19:55.683
You know what I mean?
It just seems a little unnecessary.

19:57.060 --> 20:01.105
Don't you think my esteemed colleagues
could have come up with something

20:01.147 --> 20:02.982
just a little more believable?

20:03.024 --> 20:07.403
What kind of a prank is that?
Time paradox. So uninspired.

20:09.823 --> 20:12.367
Set your device to...

20:12.408 --> 20:15.995
...2.342 and make sure
it oscillates at 11.

20:23.545 --> 20:29.300
OK, now, you... You're gonna tell me
who told you those numbers.

20:29.342 --> 20:30.510
You did.

20:31.427 --> 20:34.003
Wait a second. This is ridiculous.

20:34.055 --> 20:36.432
I know about Eloise.

20:48.444 --> 20:49.863
What is all this?

20:49.946 --> 20:53.867
This is where I do the things
Oxford frowns upon.

20:54.868 --> 20:58.121
All right, this future version of me,

20:58.163 --> 21:00.655
he referenced this meeting, right?

21:00.707 --> 21:05.253
Obviously. So I would remember
you coming to Oxford, right?

21:05.295 --> 21:07.422
I would remember this here right now.

21:07.464 --> 21:09.466
Actually... no.

21:09.507 --> 21:12.469
- No.
- Maybe you just forgot.

21:13.470 --> 21:15.555
Yeah, right. How would that happen?

21:16.890 --> 21:19.267
So this is changing the future?

21:19.309 --> 21:21.269
You can't change the future.

21:21.311 --> 21:23.636
- What's that for?
- Radiation.

21:26.316 --> 21:28.234
- Do I get one?
- You don't need one.

21:28.276 --> 21:31.279
It's for prolonged exposure.
I do this 20 times a day.

21:32.030 --> 21:33.823
So, what do you put on your head?

21:37.285 --> 21:38.536
Yeah.

21:45.168 --> 21:46.503
This...

21:47.128 --> 21:49.798
This is Eloise.

21:58.223 --> 22:00.767
- What does this do?
- This,

22:00.809 --> 22:03.217
if the numbers you gave me are correct,

22:03.269 --> 22:05.104
what this will do...

22:05.146 --> 22:09.651
...is unstick Eloise in time,
just like you.

22:26.793 --> 22:29.462
- What happened?
- Wait. She's not back yet.

22:33.550 --> 22:36.511
There she is. OK.

22:36.553 --> 22:39.222
Here goes everything.

22:41.057 --> 22:43.299
Come on, come on. Come on.

22:45.186 --> 22:48.857
That's it. Come on. That's it.

22:50.817 --> 22:52.277
Yes, yes.

22:53.069 --> 22:54.612
Yes!

23:03.163 --> 23:06.864
It worked! This is incredible.

23:06.916 --> 23:09.878
How is a rat running through a maze
so incredible?

23:09.919 --> 23:11.546
What is incredible

23:11.629 --> 23:14.799
is I just finished the maze
this morning.

23:14.841 --> 23:19.804
I'm not gonna teach her how to run it
until an hour from now.

23:26.895 --> 23:31.973
- So you sent her to the future?
- No, her consciousness. Her mind.

23:34.569 --> 23:36.529
So how does that help me?

23:36.571 --> 23:38.896
You? Help you?

23:38.948 --> 23:41.910
I don't understand. Didn't I send you
back here to help me?

23:41.951 --> 23:43.912
I don't know why you sent me here.

23:43.953 --> 23:47.123
All I know about you is you end up
on some bloody island.

23:49.125 --> 23:50.627
An island?

23:50.668 --> 23:52.712
What island? Why would I go to an...?

23:52.754 --> 23:54.380
Desmond, give me the phone.

23:55.924 --> 23:57.801
Come on, everybody relax! Listen!

23:57.842 --> 24:01.679
Daniel wanted to talk to the guy,
so we brought him the phone, that's all.

24:01.721 --> 24:04.766
- You let Faraday talk to him?
- He said he could help.

24:04.808 --> 24:07.727
- Faraday can't even help himself!
- Outside now.

24:07.769 --> 24:11.272
- The captain wants to talk to you.
- I want to talk to your captain.

24:11.356 --> 24:12.899
I'll be sure to let him know.

24:12.941 --> 24:14.734
In the meantime have a seat.

24:21.366 --> 24:23.858
- I need to get back.
- Back where? The island?

24:23.910 --> 24:26.913
He said he could help me,
tell me what I needed to do.

24:26.955 --> 24:29.582
Desmond, can you please
explain to me...?

24:29.666 --> 24:30.917
Desmond?

24:30.959 --> 24:33.253
You're Desmond?

24:34.587 --> 24:35.786
Do I know you?

24:37.048 --> 24:38.883
I'm George Minkowski.

24:38.925 --> 24:41.719
I'm the communications officer.

24:41.803 --> 24:44.013
Before they strapped me down here,

24:44.097 --> 24:48.184
all the calls to and from this boat
came through me in the radio room.

24:49.018 --> 24:51.062
And every so often...

24:51.104 --> 24:55.859
...I get this flashing light
on my console.

24:55.900 --> 25:00.978
An incoming call. We were under
strict orders never to answer it.

25:02.949 --> 25:04.951
So? What's that got to do with me?

25:04.993 --> 25:07.318
Those calls came from your girlfriend.

25:09.205 --> 25:11.124
Penelope Widmore.

25:23.678 --> 25:26.306
- What happened?
- You're back.

25:26.347 --> 25:29.934
And you were out almost 75 minutes.

25:30.643 --> 25:31.978
- Out?
- Oh, yeah.

25:32.020 --> 25:35.315
You just went catatonic
right in the middle of a sentence.

25:35.356 --> 25:39.736
I carried you to the chair. I take it
you were in the future again?

25:39.819 --> 25:40.987
Aye.

25:41.029 --> 25:43.990
- For how long?
- I don't know. Five minutes.

25:47.535 --> 25:49.537
Why does this keep happening?

25:49.579 --> 25:53.281
In your case, I'm guessing
the progression is exponential.

25:54.793 --> 25:58.546
Each time your consciousness jumps
it's harder to jump back.

25:58.588 --> 26:01.841
I would be careful crossing the street
if I were you.

26:08.264 --> 26:09.516
What happened to her?

26:09.557 --> 26:12.227
- She died.
- I can see that. How?

26:12.268 --> 26:14.145
Brain aneurysm, probably.

26:14.187 --> 26:16.231
I'm gonna do an autopsy later.

26:17.273 --> 26:21.402
- Is that gonna happen to me?
- The effects vary from case to case.

26:22.070 --> 26:26.407
Answer me! If this keeps happening,
am I gonna die?

26:28.284 --> 26:29.567
I don't know.

26:35.416 --> 26:39.202
I think Eloise's brain short-circuited.

26:39.879 --> 26:42.455
The jumps between the present
and the future,

26:42.507 --> 26:46.344
she eventually... couldn't tell
which was which. She had no anchor.

26:46.427 --> 26:50.473
- What do you mean "anchor"?
- Something familiar in both times.

26:50.515 --> 26:52.392
See this? This is all variables.

26:52.475 --> 26:56.260
It's random, it's chaotic.
Every equation needs stability,

26:56.312 --> 27:00.817
something known. It's called a constant.
Desmond, you have no constant.

27:02.402 --> 27:05.238
You go to the future
nothing new is familiar.

27:05.280 --> 27:07.657
So if you want to stop this...

27:08.283 --> 27:11.244
...then you need to find
something there,

27:11.286 --> 27:14.987
something that you really,
really care about...

27:16.458 --> 27:19.909
...that also exists back here in 1996.

27:24.174 --> 27:25.258
This constant...

27:27.218 --> 27:29.262
...can it be a person?

27:30.054 --> 27:31.598
Yeah, maybe.

27:31.639 --> 27:34.131
But you have to make
some kind of contact.

27:35.435 --> 27:38.970
I thought you said you were off
on a boat, middle of nowhere?

27:43.443 --> 27:46.654
- Who are you calling?
- I'm calling my bloody constant.

27:47.781 --> 27:50.533
<i>The number you have dialled</i>
<i>has been disconnected.</i>

27:56.331 --> 27:58.416
Hey, are you OK?

28:05.006 --> 28:07.248
You look a lot older now, huh?

28:08.593 --> 28:11.137
Welcome back, Desmond.

28:11.179 --> 28:12.378
I need to call Penny.

28:12.430 --> 28:15.058
Calling your girlfriend
is not our priority.

28:15.099 --> 28:18.353
Listen, brother, I don't know you
but you seem to know me,

28:18.394 --> 28:21.606
so if you and me are friends...

28:21.689 --> 28:23.399
...then I need your help.

28:23.441 --> 28:25.318
I need to call Penny now.

28:25.360 --> 28:27.904
You boys are getting
way ahead of yourselves.

28:27.946 --> 28:30.698
Two days ago someone
sabotaged the equipment.

28:30.740 --> 28:34.160
We lost all communication
with the mainland.

28:34.285 --> 28:36.996
I probably could've fixed it,
but then...

28:37.038 --> 28:39.707
- Then I went nuts.
- Where's the radio room?

28:39.749 --> 28:43.128
It's one deck up. I'll take you there.

28:43.169 --> 28:44.587
Come on.

28:46.506 --> 28:48.341
How do we get out of here?

28:49.134 --> 28:50.885
Through the door.

28:54.389 --> 28:57.559
Looks like you guys
have a friend on this boat.

29:05.150 --> 29:06.349
Your...

29:08.778 --> 29:09.946
Your nose, brother.

29:15.827 --> 29:17.787
It's clear.

29:18.037 --> 29:19.122
Let's...

29:35.138 --> 29:38.183
The <i>Black Rock</i> set sail
from Portsmouth, England

29:38.266 --> 29:43.229
March 22, 1845 on a trading mission
to the kingdom of Siam

29:43.271 --> 29:45.732
when she was tragically lost at sea.

29:45.773 --> 29:48.401
The only known artefact of this journey

29:48.443 --> 29:50.653
is the journal of the ship's first mate,

29:50.695 --> 29:54.908
which was discovered among the artefacts
of pirates on L'île Sainte Marie

29:54.949 --> 29:56.065
seven years later.

29:56.117 --> 30:00.622
The contents of this journal
have never been made public

30:00.663 --> 30:04.042
to anyone outside the family
of the seller, Tovard Hanso.

30:04.083 --> 30:06.836
We open the bidding on Lot 2342

30:06.878 --> 30:09.453
at £150,000.

30:10.131 --> 30:12.175
One-hundred-fifty thousand, sir.

30:12.258 --> 30:16.429
To 160? Do I hear...?
One-sixty, sir. One-seventy, sir.

30:16.471 --> 30:19.432
One-eighty on the phone.
Two hundred thousand pounds.

30:19.474 --> 30:22.352
Two-hundred-twenty thousand
pounds. Two-forty?

30:22.393 --> 30:26.231
Two-hundred-sixty thousand
pounds, sir. Two-eighty?

30:26.272 --> 30:29.067
On the phone I have 300,000...
Three-twenty.

30:29.108 --> 30:32.195
Three-hundred-forty thousand pounds.
Three-sixty?

30:32.237 --> 30:36.241
- Three-eighty.
- This auction's by appointment only.

30:36.282 --> 30:37.826
Do I hear £400,000?

30:37.867 --> 30:40.787
- Listen, I just need to speak to...
- I'm sorry, sir.

30:41.746 --> 30:46.376
Sold, for £380,000 to bidder 755.

30:46.417 --> 30:49.295
- Thank you, sir.
- Just for a minute, all right?

30:49.379 --> 30:52.298
- Look... Mr Widmore.
- Desmond.

30:52.340 --> 30:53.800
Can I have a word, sir?

30:53.842 --> 30:56.386
- I'm sorry, Mr Widmore...
- That's fine.

30:58.221 --> 30:59.639
Walk with me.

31:07.730 --> 31:09.972
Your word. Let's have it.

31:13.486 --> 31:15.530
I need to get in touch with Penny.

31:16.531 --> 31:20.660
I don't know how to reach her,
and her number's been disconnected.

31:22.412 --> 31:26.791
There was a time when, if you'd asked
her to marry you, she'd have said yes.

31:26.875 --> 31:28.835
But fortunately...

31:28.877 --> 31:31.369
...your cowardice won out instead.

31:37.635 --> 31:40.388
I take it you've had second thoughts.

31:43.224 --> 31:45.852
And you'd like her to give you
another chance.

31:46.853 --> 31:48.313
Why do you hate me so much?

31:49.772 --> 31:51.774
It's not me who hates you.

31:54.068 --> 31:56.394
Here's her address.

31:57.822 --> 32:00.283
I'll let her tell you herself.

32:18.468 --> 32:20.053
Desmond.

32:22.722 --> 32:24.599
I know. It's getting harder.

32:24.641 --> 32:27.727
It starts happening faster too.

32:29.020 --> 32:30.605
Come on, let's move.

32:33.691 --> 32:36.017
Hey, how did this happen to you?

32:37.028 --> 32:38.780
We were anchored here,

32:38.822 --> 32:42.826
waiting for our orders,
bored out of our minds.

32:43.952 --> 32:46.496
Me and Brandon,
he's one of the crew members,

32:46.579 --> 32:48.905
we took out the ship's tender.

32:50.250 --> 32:52.460
We just wanted to see the island.

32:52.502 --> 32:55.255
But Brandon started acting crazy.

32:56.506 --> 32:58.091
So we had to turn around.

32:58.133 --> 33:01.302
- Where is he?
- In a body bag.

33:06.307 --> 33:07.590
There.

33:10.603 --> 33:13.898
- Who did this?
- You got me.

33:13.940 --> 33:16.515
But when the captain finds out,
I feel sorry...

33:21.030 --> 33:24.815
After your call, someone has to tell me
precisely what is going on.

33:27.620 --> 33:30.748
- Can you fix it, brother?
- I need a minute.

33:32.959 --> 33:35.170
Do you have the number
to make the call?

33:36.546 --> 33:40.133
George, wake up, wake up.
You're going to come back.

33:40.175 --> 33:42.552
Desmond, do you know the number?

33:45.763 --> 33:48.005
- No.
- Well, you better remember it.

33:56.441 --> 33:58.735
It's 2004?

33:58.776 --> 34:01.185
I didn't realise
it was almost Christmas.

34:01.237 --> 34:02.989
It's been...

34:03.615 --> 34:05.116
Desmond.

34:09.037 --> 34:10.580
No!

34:14.000 --> 34:16.127
I... can't...

34:16.169 --> 34:18.744
...get... back.

34:30.683 --> 34:32.393
What happened to him?

34:35.522 --> 34:38.691
The same thing
that's gonna happen to me.

35:36.040 --> 35:37.125
Desmond?

35:38.877 --> 35:41.202
- What are you doing here?
- I had to.

35:41.254 --> 35:44.382
I tried to call you,
but you disconnected your phone.

35:44.424 --> 35:46.134
Yeah, because I moved.

35:47.135 --> 35:49.596
I don't know if you're
getting the signals,

35:49.637 --> 35:53.016
but I'm trying to make a clean break.
So if you don't mind...

35:53.057 --> 35:55.768
Please, I just need to get
your new phone number.

35:55.810 --> 35:58.521
- Why would I give you that?
- I made a huge mistake.

35:58.563 --> 36:02.098
I should never have broken up with you.
I know that now, I'm sorry.

36:02.150 --> 36:04.559
- Don't. Just don't do this.
- I understand.

36:04.611 --> 36:07.614
I know it's too late to change things,

36:07.655 --> 36:10.325
but I need to tell you something.

36:10.366 --> 36:13.985
I need you to listen to me.
I know it's gonna sound ridiculous,

36:14.037 --> 36:16.612
but... Please, Pen.

36:18.124 --> 36:20.043
I need you to listen to me.

36:29.177 --> 36:31.419
Just say what you need
to say and then go.

36:33.431 --> 36:37.216
I know this doesn't make sense
because it doesn't make sense to me.

36:37.268 --> 36:39.562
But eight years from now...

36:41.356 --> 36:42.607
...I need to call you.

36:42.649 --> 36:46.100
And I can't call you
if I don't have your number.

36:47.320 --> 36:50.115
- What?
- Penny, just give me your number.

36:50.198 --> 36:53.326
I know I've ruined things. I know
you think things are over,

36:53.368 --> 36:57.455
but they're not. If there's any part of
you that still believes in us, just...

36:57.539 --> 37:00.917
- ...give me your number.
- What's to say you won't call tonight?

37:00.959 --> 37:05.421
I won't call... for eight years.

37:07.757 --> 37:10.249
December 24, 2004.

37:11.386 --> 37:12.585
Christmas Eve.

37:14.931 --> 37:16.474
I promise.

37:19.394 --> 37:21.062
Please, Pen.

37:24.232 --> 37:26.724
If I give you the number,
will you leave?

37:27.360 --> 37:28.695
Aye.

37:35.577 --> 37:38.955
7946-0893.

37:41.166 --> 37:43.001
7946-0893. 7946...

37:43.042 --> 37:45.712
All that, and you're not gonna
write it down?

37:48.590 --> 37:50.383
It wouldn't do any good.

37:51.968 --> 37:54.179
You have to keep that number.

37:54.220 --> 37:58.057
- Please get out! Get out!
- Just remember, December 24, 2004.

37:58.099 --> 38:00.810
If you still care about me,
you have to answer.

38:00.852 --> 38:03.261
I'm not crazy, Penny!
You have to believe me!

38:03.313 --> 38:05.690
You have to trust me!

38:05.773 --> 38:07.775
I do trust you.

38:07.817 --> 38:10.393
But you still have to remember
that number.

38:12.781 --> 38:15.189
7946-0893.

38:15.241 --> 38:16.701
7946-0893.

38:16.743 --> 38:19.204
7946-0893. It's a London number.

38:19.245 --> 38:20.622
Excellent timing.

38:22.499 --> 38:24.000
The patch is done,

38:24.042 --> 38:26.753
but I don't know how long
the battery will last.

38:29.881 --> 38:31.163
I hope she's there.

38:31.925 --> 38:33.468
I hope so too.

39:10.338 --> 39:12.382
<i>Hello?</i>

39:14.300 --> 39:16.709
Penny?

39:16.761 --> 39:18.429
<i>Desmond?</i>

39:29.899 --> 39:31.943
Penny. Penny, you answered.

39:33.570 --> 39:35.029
You answered, Penny.

39:38.450 --> 39:39.784
Des, where are you?

39:40.994 --> 39:43.319
I'm...

39:44.539 --> 39:47.500
I'm... I'm on a boat...

39:49.377 --> 39:52.213
I've... I've been on an island and...

39:54.466 --> 39:57.260
- Oh, my God, Penny, is that really you?
- Yeah.

39:58.136 --> 39:59.220
Yes, it's me.

40:02.432 --> 40:03.516
You believed me.

40:05.518 --> 40:08.271
You still care about me.

40:08.313 --> 40:11.816
Des, I've been looking for you
for the past three years.

40:11.858 --> 40:15.309
I know about the island.
I've been researching...

40:17.739 --> 40:20.450
<i>...and then when I spoke</i>
<i>to your friend Charlie</i>,

40:20.492 --> 40:24.788
that's when I knew you were still alive.
That's when I knew I wasn't crazy.

40:27.791 --> 40:30.460
- Des, are you still there?
- Yes, yes, I'm here.

40:30.502 --> 40:33.755
- I'm still here. Can you hear me?
- Yeah, that's better.

40:34.839 --> 40:36.883
I love you, Penny.

40:39.511 --> 40:41.221
I've always loved you.

40:43.306 --> 40:44.557
I'm so sorry.

40:47.185 --> 40:49.343
I love you.

40:49.395 --> 40:50.480
I love you too.

40:51.022 --> 40:53.264
- I don't know where I am.
- I'll find you.

40:53.316 --> 40:55.401
- I promise... I'll come back.
- No matter what.

40:55.443 --> 40:57.602
- I won't give up, I promise.
- I promise.

40:57.654 --> 40:59.155
- I love you.
- I love you.

41:10.208 --> 41:13.711
I'm sorry. The power source
went dead. That's all we had.

41:23.763 --> 41:26.141
Thank you, Sayid.

41:30.645 --> 41:32.397
It was enough.

41:35.191 --> 41:37.193
Are you all right now?

41:40.113 --> 41:41.229
Aye.

41:42.490 --> 41:44.075
I'm perfect.
